---
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';

const SCHEDULING_LINK = "https://calendar.app.google/ZgCjgA8Mk3tosTmh9";
---

<MarketingLayout
	title="Work | People Purpose Product"
	description="Three ways I take the product owner seat on funded mission-driven teams: a product studio, a fractional seat, and coaching for the person already doing the job."
>
	<section class="page-header">
		<h1>Work</h1>
		<p class="lede">
			You know your impact space better than any consultant will. You have funding, and
			now you can go build without waiting on a hire. That part is new, and it's good.
		</p>
		<p class="lede">
			Backlogs and milestones are the easy part. The hard part is deciding where to
			invest, and moving before you have all the information you'd like. That's the
			gap I work in, in three shapes, depending on what you already have.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="services">
		<article class="service">
			<h2>Product studio</h2>
			<p class="what">
				I own the roadmap and bring the engineers. You get a working product, and a team
				that can tell you why it was built this way and not some other way.
			</p>
			<p class="fit"><b>Fits when</b> you have funding and a real problem, and nobody inside to run the build.</p>
		</article>

		<article class="service">
			<h2>Fractional product owner</h2>
			<p class="what">
				I take the product owner seat on your team, and the roadmap stays yours. I'm in
				the meetings: drafting the requirements, designing the experiments, reading what
				comes back, making the call with your people in the room.
			</p>
			<p class="fit"><b>Fits when</b> you already have engineers, and nobody deciding what they build.</p>
		</article>

		<article class="service">
			<h2>Product owner coaching</h2>
			<p class="what">
				For the person already doing this job without the title. We draft the roadmap
				together, run the experiments together, and sit in it together when an idea
				flops. Then you keep doing it after I'm gone.
			</p>
			<p class="fit"><b>Fits when</b> someone on your team has the instincts and has never had anyone to learn the craft from.</p>
		</article>
	</section>

	<section class="content-section">
		<h2>The studio and the fractional seat look alike from outside</h2>
		<p>
			They mostly are alike. The difference is who owns the roadmap. In the studio I own
			it. In the fractional seat you own it, and I sit in it with you.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="content-section">
		<h2>How I work</h2>
		<p>
			I can do it for you. I can teach you how. What I actually want is to do it with
			you: draft the roadmap together, run the experiment, be uncomfortable together and
			watch our ideas flop.
		</p>
		<p>
			The flopping is the part people skip, and it's the part that pays. A client of mine
			wanted a chatbot to handle one step of their flow. We looked at it together and
			realized a plain form would do that same job correctly every single time. The
			chatbot's real use turned out to be telling us which steps should have been forms
			all along. That's a smaller product than the one we started with, and a better one,
			and no amount of prompting would have gotten us there.
		</p>
		<p>
			Every engagement ends the same way. Your team can do this without me.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="content-section closing">
		<h2>Start a conversation</h2>
		<p>
			If any of this resonates, I'd love to talk. Book 30 minutes and tell me what
			you're working on.
		</p>
		<a href={SCHEDULING_LINK} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="cta-button">
			Find a time →
		</a>
		<p class="schedule-note">
			Prefer email? Write me at <a class="email-link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/nicknorena/">hello at this domain</a>.
		</p>
	</section>
</MarketingLayout>

<script>
	// Assemble the address in the browser so scrapers reading the raw HTML
	// never see a complete email. The href above is a fallback (LinkedIn)
	// for the rare no-JS visitor.
	const user = 'hello';
	const domain = 'peoplepurposeproduct.com';
	const address = `${user}@${domain}`;
	document.querySelectorAll('.email-link').forEach((el) => {
		el.setAttribute('href', `mailto:${address}`);
		el.textContent = address;
	});
</script>

<style>
	.page-header {
		padding: 3em 0 2.5em;
		border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
		margin-bottom: 3em;
	}
	.page-header h1 {
		font-size: 3rem;
		line-height: 1.1;
	}
	.page-header .lede {
		margin-top: 1em;
		max-width: 720px;
		font-size: 1.1rem;
		line-height: 1.6;
	}

	.services {
		display: grid;
		gap: 2.5em;
		margin-bottom: 3em;
		padding-bottom: 3em;
		border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
	}
	.service {
		max-width: 720px;
	}
	.service h2 {
		font-size: 1.375rem;
		margin: 0 0 0.4em;
	}
	.service .what {
		margin: 0 0 0.6em;
	}
	.service .fit {
		margin: 0;
		color: rgb(var(--gray));
		font-size: 0.95rem;
	}

	.content-section {
		margin-bottom: 3em;
		padding-bottom: 3em;
		border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
		max-width: 720px;
	}
	.content-section h2 {
		font-size: 1.5rem;
		margin-bottom: 0.75em;
	}
	.closing {
		border-bottom: none;
	}

	.cta-button {
		display: inline-block;
		margin-top: 0.5em;
		padding: 0.75em 1.5em;
		background: var(--accent);
		color: white;
		text-decoration: none;
		border-radius: 8px;
		font-weight: 700;
	}
	.cta-button:hover {
		background: var(--accent-dark);
		color: white;
	}
	.schedule-note {
		margin-top: 1.25em;
		color: rgb(var(--gray));
		font-size: 0.95rem;
	}

	@media (max-width: 720px) {
		.page-header h1 {
			font-size: 2.25rem;
		}
	}
</style>
